{"id":"982tatv2","parent":"mtyky6kw","ord":"a0","title":"watch","desc":"The watcher's knobs, read live by the olai server.\n\n`nag` CARRIES ITS CAP: `30m/3` means every thirty minutes, three reminders after the first report, then quiet about that terminal until its state changes — the human's ruling of 2026-09-03 (\"a finite nag, three reminders\"), shipped by #489 and set here 2026-09-12 after the knob file was renamed from `_olai/Kolu.olai` and the value did not travel with it, which is why the nag had gone uncapped again. A bare `30m` would repeat forever. The grammar is kolu's own `parseNag`, so a bare number is refused with a sentence rather than run as milliseconds.","created":"2026-09-11T15:52:25-04:00","changed":"2026-09-12T12:13:11-04:00","custom":{"heartbeat":"6h","nag":"30m/3"}}
